Bundled speech engines (only in apps packaged with --speech-bundle)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
An app built with scripts/build_speech_bundle.py ships these unmodified
third-party components in Contents/Resources/speech. Each runs as a separate
process. Exact pins are in services/speech-bundle/manifest.json; the installed
Python distributions and their license files are recorded in
speech/evidence/freeze.txt and speech/evidence/distributions.json.

- CPython 3.12 (python-build-standalone): PSF License 2.0 and bundled
  third-party notices, speech/python/lib/python3.12/LICENSE.txt.
- Kokoro-82M model and English voices (hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, revision
  f3ff3571791e39611d31c381e3a41a3af07b4987): Apache-2.0 per the model card.
  The kokoro, misaki, torch, numpy, spaCy and en_core_web_sm packages keep
  their own licenses in their installed dist-info folders.
- Piper (piper-tts 1.8.0, https://github.com/OHF-voice/piper1-gpl):
  GPL-3.0-or-later, embedding eSpeak NG (GPL-3.0-or-later). License text:
  piper_tts-1.8.0.data/data/COPYING in the installed package. Corresponding
  source: the upstream repository at tag v1.8.0 and the PyPI sdist
  piper_tts-1.8.0.tar.gz. Public distribution must also meet GPL-3.0 source
  obligations (see docs/bundled-speech.md).
- Finnish voice fi_FI-harri-medium (rhasspy/piper-voices, revision
  b4e358ffcb232591bf73a540e70f7de528e4174a): repository tagged MIT; the voice
  card names a CC0 dataset; speech/piper/MODEL_CARD.
- Rhubarb Lip Sync 1.14.0 (https://github.com/DanielSWolf/rhubarb-lip-sync):
  MIT, with CMU PocketSphinx/Sphinxbase (BSD-style) acoustic and language
  models; speech/rhubarb/LICENSE.md.

These entries record what is shipped. They are not a completed legal review
of every transitive dependency; see docs/bundled-speech.md.
